A triplet of bases codes for one amino acid. This fact only partly explains how the activity of gene *ABCA3*, which is 80 kb long, can result in the protein ABCA3, which is only 1704 amino acids long.

Suggest **other** reasons to explain the difference in the number of base pairs in gene *ABCA3* compared with the number of amino acids in protein ABCA3.

